import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Transparency | AndrexTheDev"
  description="Zero-data architecture: no accounts, no tracking cookies, local browser storage with one-click deletion — AndrexTheDev."
  heading="Privacy Transparency"
>
  <h2>1. Zero-data architecture</h2>
  <p>
    The Suite is consistently built so that personal data does not arise at the operator in the first place:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No user accounts:</strong> there is no registration, no login and no session management by the operator.</li>
    <li><strong>No tracking cookies:</strong> no cookies are set.</li>
    <li><strong>No analytics scripts:</strong> there are no external analytics, counting-pixel or fingerprinting services.</li>
    <li><strong>No server logs of wallet inputs:</strong> addresses, transaction data and check inputs are processed locally in the browser and not transmitted to any infrastructure of the operator.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Local storage in the browser</h2>
  <p>
    For functional reasons the Suite uses only browser-side storage locations:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>localStorage:</strong> optionally self-configured network endpoints (key prefixes <code>atd-</code> and <code>ds-rpc-</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>IndexedDB:</strong> short-lived read cache for blockchain responses and pausable scan progress (e.g. time-boxed stealth scans).</li>
  </ul>
  <p id="lokal">
    This data does not leave your device through the Suite and can be deleted at any time with one click:
    via <strong>Network &amp; data sources → "Delete all local suite data"</strong> in the navigation bar.
    Alternatively you can remove the website data in your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Direct browser connections to blockchain endpoints</h2>
  <p>
    When you use a tool in online mode, <strong>your browser directly</strong> sends read requests (JSON-RPC) to
    network endpoints — preferably to endpoints you have configured, alternatively rotating across publicly reachable
    read endpoints. The following applies:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The endpoint operator sees your IP address and the queried public data (e.g. an address or a transaction hash).</li>
    <li>There is <strong>no</strong> transmission of private keys or seed phrases — the Suite does not accept such input and actively blocks recognized patterns.</li>
    <li>You can limit network exposure by configuring your own endpoints or by using the offline modes of the tools (manual entry of raw data, file upload).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Wallet connections</h2>
  <p>
    Optional wallet connections (EIP-1193/EIP-6963) take place exclusively upon your explicit action and
    exclusively between your browser and your wallet software. The Suite only receives the data you release in the
    wallet (e.g. a public address, the signature of a challenge).
  </p>

  <h2>5. Email contact</h2>
  <p>
    When contacting <strong>hippie.highho@gmail.com</strong> by email, the operator processes the data
    transmitted with the email (sender, content, metadata) to handle the request. The legal basis is
    Art.&nbsp;6(1)(b) or Art.&nbsp;6(1)(f) GDPR. Requests are deleted once they have been dealt with,
    unless statutory retention obligations exist.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent personal data is processed by the operator (essentially email communication), you have
    the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability and
    objection. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the competent data protection supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    Controller within the meaning of the GDPR: <strong>AndrexTheDev</strong>, reachable by email:
    <strong>hippie.highho@gmail.com</strong>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
